! mcp_bootstrap_p222.strap -- MCP printed page 222: the Input Program's
! scratch/queue section (V SCEND .. V REQ), lines 1-50.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.229, read at 400 dpi, 900 dpi for
! doubtful glyphs.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID CA000378  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 222"; the heading
! row's LOCATION field is 224430, line 1's word.
!
! THE PAGE.  50 lines, every one located, contiguous from 224430.00 to
! 224461.40 (a half word; next word 224462.00, where the p.223 scratch
! deck opens), except lines 43-44, two
! SYNs printed at 224110.00+ / 224110.40+ (BU,04,10 -- V VSCR's (BU,4)
! carried through).  p.221 ends at 224427.40, so line 1 joins it.
! Remarks -0389 .. -0433; lines 4, 16, 27, 30, 31, 37, 39, 40, 45 print
! none (no -0403, -0416, -0423, -0424 appear).
!
! CARD SERIALS 0A000378 .. 0A000422 (prefix printed with the round
! glyph; p.221 reads its prefix DA), 45 serials for 50 lines: five pairs
! share one -- lines 4/5 (381), 27/28 (403), 30/31 (405), 37/38 (411),
! 45/46 (418), each a SIC or B,D MCP plus its half word.  Asterisks
! after the LOCATION on lines 16 and 36.
!
! GLYPHS.  Labels V QQ, V QQ2, V QQ1, V QEND print their Q's worn toward
! G/C at 400 dpi; at 900 dpi every one shows the tail inside the bowl,
! as the references B,V QQ2 / BXVZ,VQQ1 / LVNI,V T2,V QEND print it,
! and the binaries (224453.10, 224456.31, 224457.15) are those labels.
! V QEND at 224457.00 is p.221's VQEND (LVNI 224457.23).  V SCEND's last
! glyph (label and line 1) has the squared corners of a D, unlike the
! round C beside it.  "V CCM" (line 36) is V COM: its second glyph is
! squared like the O of V BYON; B prints 224702.10 = VCOM.  "V PCP" is
! V POP, "V PDQ" reads with a D stem.  V RBLC's last glyph is round: C.
! Octal-field opens ("C00000.CC", "224626.C3") are 0.  HEX BYTES
! printed with an open round, written 0: line 1 "C9" (LVNI: line 48
! and p.221 line 24 print 09), lines 2/6 "C1" (LVI, as lines 21/23/47
! print 01), line 3 "C0" (B with no index is 00, as lines 30/33 print
! it), line 25 "FC" (CM0000 second half is F0; p.18 rule).  The C of
! C8 (line 12) and C9 (41, 49) is CB-'s op nibble and real; D0 (line
! 24, SVA) shows a D stem.  All settled by what the statement assembles
! to; every row PASSES.  Statement "CMOCOO" (line 25) is CM0000.

